@page "/ui"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@*
   AllowAnonymous is here ONLY because this page carries no data and exists to
   prove the scaffold renders. Everything else inherits the host's fallback
   authorization policy, which is what makes an unauthenticated request to a
   Blazor route return 401 rather than content — verified, and the behaviour we
   want.

   REAL SCREENS MUST NOT COPY THIS. TFND-61 replaces this page with the
   primitives gallery; the attribute goes with it.

   Related: an unauthenticated browser currently gets a JSON 401 here rather
   than a sign-in challenge. That is TFND-126's problem, not the scaffold's.
*@

@* Proves the scaffold end to end: the RCL is discovered by the host, the route
   table works, static assets resolve, and an interactive server circuit opens
   and round-trips. Replaced by the primitives gallery in TFND-61. *@

<PageTitle>tamp.findings — scaffold</PageTitle>

<h1>tamp<span class="accent">.findings</span></h1>
<p class="kicker">blazor scaffold · TFND-60</p>

<p>
    Render mode: <code>InteractiveServer</code>.
    Circuit round-trips: <code>@_clicks</code>
</p>
<button class="btn" @onclick="() => _clicks++">Prove the circuit</button>

@code {
    private int _clicks;
}
